# the real run's LLM cache is the checkpoint for a multi-hour generation
# run - losing it means losing hours of model time. Smoke caches stay ignored.
!.cache/llm/
!.cache/llm/responses.jsonl

# the answerability judge's cache is a separate OllamaClient/cache pair from
# generate_json's -- it must never collide with .cache/llm/'s checkpoint
# (same (model, prompt) key, different response shape: free text vs JSON).
# Not negated: unlike .cache/llm/, it is a disposable re-run cache, not a
# checkpoint worth committing.
.cache/judge/

# raw measurement artifacts behind handbook/eval-of-evals.md's claims -
# a number without a reproducible artifact is an assertion
!run/item_analysis.json
!run/matrix200.json
